<h2>Which grouped layout fits the settings page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Same 12 fields in all three, split into Profile, Preferences, Notifications, and Security. Click to pick one.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Settings</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px">
          <div class="label">Profile</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL">
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Preferences</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Time zone"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Language"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Theme">
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Notifications</div>
          <div>[x] Email &nbsp; [ ] Push &nbsp; [x] Weekly digest</div>
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Security</div>
          <div>[x] Two-factor auth</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Session timeout (min)"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="API token">
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Stacked sections</h3>
      <p>One page, headed fieldsets in sequence, one Save. Smallest change; everything still visible at once.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Settings</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px">
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px">
            <div class="placeholder" style="text-align:left"><b>Profile</b><br>Display name<br>Email<br>Avatar URL</div>
            <div class="placeholder" style="text-align:left"><b>Preferences</b><br>Time zone<br>Language<br>Theme</div>
            <div class="placeholder" style="text-align:left"><b>Notifications</b><br>[x] Email<br>[ ] Push<br>[x] Digest</div>
            <div class="placeholder" style="text-align:left"><b>Security</b><br>[x] 2FA<br>Session timeout<br>API token</div>
          </div>
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Card grid</h3>
      <p>Each group in its own card, 2x2 on wide screens, stacking on narrow ones. Very scannable; needs a wider container than today's 640px.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Settings</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px">
            <div class="mock-sidebar" style="min-width:90px"><b>Profile</b><br>Preferences<br>Notifications<br>Security</div>
            <div class="mock-content" style="flex:1">
              <div class="label">Profile</div>
              <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL">
              <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Side nav / tabs</h3>
      <p>One group visible at a time. Scales to many more settings, but hides fields and needs JS for switching.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
